# Review handoff

Each review report updates the Now / Next / Open decisions block in
`docs/README.md` in the same change. That block is the single source for
current work. See `docs/reviews/README.md` for the report conventions.

When Zach approves an increment, or asks for the wrap-up, give both of these
in the same reply. Do not start the next increment in that reply.

1. **Commit message.** One or two sentences that say why the change exists.
   Do not commit unless Zach asks.
2. **Next-chat prompt.** A paste-ready block that names `AGENTS.md`,
   `docs/README.md`, the latest review, `docs/reviews/README.md`, and the
   pending decision or next roadmap item. A new chat should be able to start
   from those files alone.

Before writing that prompt, compare the item it would name with
`docs/roadmap.md`. The plan is out of order when that item would skip an
earlier item in the same phase, or an earlier phase item the roadmap still
lists as not started. An inserted section the roadmap places before that
earlier item is in order. Skipping past it is not.

When it is out of order, stop before the prompt. Name the earlier items
that are still open and the later item the prompt would start. Ask Zach
whether he knows the plan is out of order and wants to continue with that
later work. Ask again before every later prompt that would skip those
items. A yes on one prompt does not cover the next handoff. Write the
prompt only after he says to continue. If he says no, the prompt names
the earliest open item instead.

On October 8, 2026, Phase 2 items 7 and 8 were still not started when a
prompt said to start Phase 3. That prompt should have waited for a yes.

Stay in the current chat if the increment is unfinished or the reasoning is
not in the repository yet.
